# Grok-Only Tonight Rule

- Cursor/Grok is the only coding provider tonight.
- Local Qwen and Codex fallback are disabled.
- Never guess the Cursor CLI model id.
- Require installed/authenticated Cursor CLI and exact model resolution before unattended start.
- Primary repo may remain dirty only if it is controller-only and all coding targets a separate clean isolated worktree.
- Grok receives file read/write capability only; deny Shell, WebFetch and MCP.
- NightToolHost runs acceptance commands.
- Fresh Cursor process per task.
- Provider/quota failure stops the run cleanly; do not switch models.
- No commit, push, reset, clean, merge, or worktree deletion automatically.
